## Six APIs, one portal

{% card-grid %}
{% card title="Rates" icon="currency-eur" href="/apis/rates" %}
Public prices and service levels. No sign-in needed; try it right below.
{% /card %}
{% card title="Shipments" icon="package" href="/apis/shipments" %}
Create, list and cancel shipments, print labels, receive webhooks. For shop developers.
{% /card %}
{% card title="Tracking" icon="map-pin" href="/apis/tracking" %}
Parcel events and push subscriptions, with OAuth or an API key.
{% /card %}
{% card title="Carrier Partners" icon="truck" href="/apis/carriers" %}
Manifests, label uploads and pickups for partner carriers.
{% /card %}
{% /card-grid %}

{% callout type="lock" title="Two more behind sign-in" %}
The **Billing** and **Admin** APIs are internal. They appear in the [catalog](/catalog/) with a lock until you [sign in](/docs/authentication/) with a role that may read them.
{% /callout %}

## Quote a parcel now

The Rates API is public, so this console works without signing in. It sends the request to the mock server (`rapidoc mock`) on your machine.

{% api-operation spec="rates" path="/rates" method="get" /%}
